## Oceanside Lemon Law and Used Vehicles

California is one of the few states in the country that provides lemon law benefits for used vehicles - but there are several things to know about the process:

## Dealer Warranties

Many vehicles sold at used car dealerships in California come with dealer warranties. These are much shorter than original manufacturer warranties that come with new vehicles - generally good for 30 days after purchase or before 1,000 miles accrue on the odometer.

If a used vehicle meets the qualifications of California lemon law within the terms of the dealer warranty, you may file a lemon law claim in the same manner as a new vehicle.

“As Is” Agreements

“As is” agreements usually mean there are no California lemon law rights in place - and the consumer takes complete responsibility for any defects after purchase. “As is” agreements should be displayed on the used vehicle’s buyer’s guide.

If the buyer’s guide does not specify a dealer warranty or “as is” agreement, there may be an [implied warranty of merchantability](https://codes.findlaw.com/ca/civil-code/civ-sect-1791-1/) in effect. This is an unspoken agreement that the vehicle is fit for its intended use - and typically covers the essential components. You will need a skilled lemon law attorney in Oceanside to fight for your rights under an implied warranty.

